 & =\\frac{2}{1-(-x)^{2}}\\cdot (-x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1-{x}^{2}}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20a149cb-038d-5c18-bde3-ae3a967e2c4f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20a149cb-038d-5c18-bde3-ae3a967e2c4f" :answer-field/id #uuid "20a149cb-038d-5c18-bde3-ae3a967e2c4f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-07693188-9e0b-5dc7-8381-dfa9941382ce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-07693188-9e0b-5dc7-8381-dfa9941382ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07693188-9e0b-5dc7-8381-dfa9941382ce" :answer/id #uuid "07693188-9e0b-5dc7-8381-dfa9941382ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x^{2}-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-31ce7adb-3732-5d9f-92f5-a50363ba4c8e" :question/id #uuid "31ce7adb-3732-5d9f-92f5-a50363ba4c8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-95547" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f722b7c-71a8-54c2-bd1f-6c40dfef6193"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f722b7c-71a8-54c2-bd1f-6c40dfef6193" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f722b7c-71a8-54c2-bd1f-6c40dfef6193" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a28440b4-85d4-5314-bd6f-4661a409d1f7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fa7a3b35-80dc-562d-8811-ba107d45cb51" "answer-fa166499-b1c8-5634-aac0-e2d68fea0b82" "answer-a28440b4-85d4-5314-bd6f-4661a409d1f7" "answer-04767459-77d9-53e0-8f3a-4e50f91b46c1" "answer-6440a19f-723d-54fa-8469-a5e28443074d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa7a3b35-80dc-562d-8811-ba107d45cb51" :answer/id #uuid "fa7a3b35-80dc-562d-8811-ba107d45cb51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa166499-b1c8-5634-aac0-e2d68fea0b82" :answer/id #uuid "fa166499-b1c8-5634-aac0-e2d68fea0b82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a28440b4-85d4-5314-bd6f-4661a409d1f7" :answer/id #uuid "a28440b4-85d4-5314-bd6f-4661a409d1f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04767459-77d9-53e0-8f3a-4e50f91b46c1" :answer/id #uuid "04767459-77d9-53e0-8f3a-4e50f91b46c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6440a19f-723d-54fa-8469-a5e28443074d" :answer/id #uuid "6440a19f-723d-54fa-8469-a5e28443074d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{tan}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7b99a120-8ee4-5c4d-80c5-2291fb8275da" :question/id #uuid "7b99a120-8ee4-5c4d-80c5-2291fb8275da" :question/math-academy-id "q-313249" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)},$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\frac{1}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1).$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nand the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1))^{′}=\\frac{1}{1-(2x-1)^{2}}\\cdot (2x-1)^{′}=\\frac{2}{4x-4{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(4x-4{x}^{2})\\,{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(2x-1)}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4x-4{x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{1}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡(2x-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-697491e1-d5eb-582f-b6a9-c05cd0efc616"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-697491e1-d5eb-582f-b6a9-c05cd0efc616" :answer-field/id #uuid "697491e1-d5eb-582f-b6a9-c05cd0efc616" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-15d81d09-9d4d-5817-aef8-323fc9bab399" :answer-field/choices ["answer-15d81d09-9d4d-5817-aef8-323fc9bab399"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-15d81d09-9d4d-5817-aef8-323fc9bab399" :answer/id #uuid "15d81d09-9d4d-5817-aef8-323fc9bab399" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{4x-4{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9939cec3-a9a6-5501-8d65-e82136850623" :question/id #uuid "9939cec3-a9a6-5501-8d65-e82136850623" :question/math-academy-id "q-95558" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}+g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{arcoth}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61946e48-e92a-5775-b260-b027052600f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61946e48-e92a-5775-b260-b027052600f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "61946e48-e92a-5775-b260-b027052600f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5d2dd98c-0888-5e14-a9da-7bfa796c8fcc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5d2dd98c-0888-5e14-a9da-7bfa796c8fcc" "answer-9d4b0471-37b3-54f6-a468-ae5368af1054" "answer-68314971-85df-5e1a-bb8d-30df1853ed17" "answer-2e708ed0-211d-5ee2-b1e8-74d164752177" "answer-154fd44c-1903-5cec-bc2f-cfb042f862e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d2dd98c-0888-5e14-a9da-7bfa796c8fcc" :answer/id #uuid "5d2dd98c-0888-5e14-a9da-7bfa796c8fcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d4b0471-37b3-54f6-a468-ae5368af1054" :answer/id #uuid "9d4b0471-37b3-54f6-a468-ae5368af1054" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2})\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68314971-85df-5e1a-bb8d-30df1853ed17" :answer/id #uuid "68314971-85df-5e1a-bb8d-30df1853ed17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}{arcoth}^{2}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e708ed0-211d-5ee2-b1e8-74d164752177" :answer/id #uuid "2e708ed0-211d-5ee2-b1e8-74d164752177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{(1-{x}^{2}){arcoth}^{2}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-154fd44c-1903-5cec-bc2f-cfb042f862e3" :answer/id #uuid "154fd44c-1903-5cec-bc2f-cfb042f862e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-54c54e62-4a18-5ab6-878d-ec4e2ae2aaa7" :question/id #uuid "54c54e62-4a18-5ab6-878d-ec4e2ae2aaa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341554" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x,$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x}{x}\\,-$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a product $u(x)\\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡x\\,+\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3d13f910-7112-5195-9bff-e3f1ef20780b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d13f910-7112-5195-9bff-e3f1ef20780b" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d13f910-7112-5195-9bff-e3f1ef20780b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b29336a1-2d9f-50d2-a125-62f689031329" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b29336a1-2d9f-50d2-a125-62f689031329"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b29336a1-2d9f-50d2-a125-62f689031329" :answer/id #uuid "b29336a1-2d9f-50d2-a125-62f689031329" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\ln x}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3337e5e0-9e46-58ca-9b60-fe0a52d9614e" :question/id #uuid "3337e5e0-9e46-58ca-9b60-fe0a52d9614e" :question/math-academy-id "q-341550" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(x)}{\\sqrt{x}},$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}($ \n{{field-1}} $-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x})$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(x)$ and $v(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{{[v(x)]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′}}{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot {(\\sqrt{x})}^{′}}{x} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{2x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-584b1c26-caed-504f-b964-753688b3a2ed"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-584b1c26-caed-504f-b964-753688b3a2ed" :answer-field/id #uuid "584b1c26-caed-504f-b964-753688b3a2ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-39c346e6-1707-5c7d-ba00-77662529622f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39c346e6-1707-5c7d-ba00-77662529622f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-39c346e6-1707-5c7d-ba00-77662529622f" :answer/id #uuid "39c346e6-1707-5c7d-ba00-77662529622f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096610 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-451b7f5e-73c7-5775-8944-779b29e93099" "question-9cb89f9e-c6cf-5b21-994c-7efe5115b691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096611 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c8792aa5-0567-5ee4-a5c8-0188d2815575"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096612 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-46572da3-e0a7-57d7-a2f6-062b0d2adadb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-451b7f5e-73c7-5775-8944-779b29e93099" :question/id #uuid "451b7f5e-73c7-5775-8944-779b29e93099" :question/math-academy-id "q-340053" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=9{e}^{x}-11,$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $-11$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nUsing the addition rule, then, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x}-11) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-11) \\\\  & =9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =9{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-321e32b9-7ce0-5a4e-9141-f36ce7923b8b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-321e32b9-7ce0-5a4e-9141-f36ce7923b8b" :answer-field/id #uuid "321e32b9-7ce0-5a4e-9141-f36ce7923b8b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-53709e9e-7e4f-52ba-ab20-e6b13619abb3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-53709e9e-7e4f-52ba-ab20-e6b13619abb3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53709e9e-7e4f-52ba-ab20-e6b13619abb3" :answer/id #uuid "53709e9e-7e4f-52ba-ab20-e6b13619abb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9e^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9cb89f9e-c6cf-5b21-994c-7efe5115b691" :question/id #uuid "9cb89f9e-c6cf-5b21-994c-7efe5115b691" :question/math-academy-id "q-304018" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=4{e}^{x}+17$, the slope of the tangent line at $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $17$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nFirst, using the addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}+17) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(17) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} & ={(4{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =4{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ff484f27-c600-5f6e-a8a7-362f170f3f67"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ff484f27-c600-5f6e-a8a7-362f170f3f67" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff484f27-c600-5f6e-a8a7-362f170f3f67" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-25800a6b-d642-5c57-b91d-e8e45649680a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25800a6b-d642-5c57-b91d-e8e45649680a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25800a6b-d642-5c57-b91d-e8e45649680a" :answer/id #uuid "25800a6b-d642-5c57-b91d-e8e45649680a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c8792aa5-0567-5ee4-a5c8-0188d2815575" :question/id #uuid "c8792aa5-0567-5ee4-a5c8-0188d2815575" :question/math-academy-id "q-71061" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=4{e}^{x}-5{x}^{3}-4$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-5{x}^{3}-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-5(3{x}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-15{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb8c7399-82f9-563a-b941-a6a1414975f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb8c7399-82f9-563a-b941-a6a1414975f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb8c7399-82f9-563a-b941-a6a1414975f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f62c6064-bf12-5a1a-94a5-4dec0bfb8ced" :answer-field/choices ["answer-abe87bd5-4230-5c4c-a3fa-4e14394a9de6" "answer-f62c6064-bf12-5a1a-94a5-4dec0bfb8ced" "answer-13a8ae5e-2b27-5896-8bf1-0e1c78f29b99" "answer-c7f7e59c-61a8-51bc-b810-b28f0b8fe05c" "answer-a76babff-69cc-5977-a846-865ec261880c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-abe87bd5-4230-5c4c-a3fa-4e14394a9de6" :answer/id #uuid "abe87bd5-4230-5c4c-a3fa-4e14394a9de6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)=4{e}^{x}-10x-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f62c6064-bf12-5a1a-94a5-4dec0bfb8ced" :answer/id #uuid "f62c6064-bf12-5a1a-94a5-4dec0bfb8ced" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)=4{e}^{x}-15{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13a8ae5e-2b27-5896-8bf1-0e1c78f29b99" :answer/id #uuid "13a8ae5e-2b27-5896-8bf1-0e1c78f29b99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)=4{e}^{x}-5{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7f7e59c-61a8-51bc-b810-b28f0b8fe05c" :answer/id #uuid "c7f7e59c-61a8-51bc-b810-b28f0b8fe05c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}-15{x}^{2}-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a76babff-69cc-5977-a846-865ec261880c" :answer/id #uuid "a76babff-69cc-5977-a846-865ec261880c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(x)={e}^{x}-9x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-46572da3-e0a7-57d7-a2f6-062b0d2adadb" :question/id #uuid "46572da3-e0a7-57d7-a2f6-062b0d2adadb" :question/math-academy-id "q-140439" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=4\\cdot {2}^{x}+{x}^{3}-{e}^{2}$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\cdot {2}^{x}+{x}^{3}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\cdot {2}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+0 \\\\  & =4\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & =(4\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3{x}^{2}){|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =4\\cdot {2}^{0}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3\\cdot {0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2+3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-552b41e9-7a71-51a8-a342-aa77b81b7fa3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-552b41e9-7a71-51a8-a342-aa77b81b7fa3" :answer-field/id #uuid "552b41e9-7a71-51a8-a342-aa77b81b7fa3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f466827c-355f-5cbc-b5b1-a9351be94db5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-83f09c8c-036c-5988-8f2a-b6776804e7ba" "answer-f466827c-355f-5cbc-b5b1-a9351be94db5" "answer-ddfba5da-de74-5003-94d8-2da062180d72" "answer-0caca0a6-1e08-5ddf-bb83-3bec4e2484b5" "answer-29c8efb8-570d-51ab-b67b-d69348dbbf78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83f09c8c-036c-5988-8f2a-b6776804e7ba" :answer/id #uuid "83f09c8c-036c-5988-8f2a-b6776804e7ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f466827c-355f-5cbc-b5b1-a9351be94db5" :answer/id #uuid "f466827c-355f-5cbc-b5b1-a9351be94db5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddfba5da-de74-5003-94d8-2da062180d72" :answer/id #uuid "ddfba5da-de74-5003-94d8-2da062180d72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0caca0a6-1e08-5ddf-bb83-3bec4e2484b5" :answer/id #uuid "0caca0a6-1e08-5ddf-bb83-3bec4e2484b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-2e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29c8efb8-570d-51ab-b67b-d69348dbbf78" :answer/id #uuid "29c8efb8-570d-51ab-b67b-d69348dbbf78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-4e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186297290 :question/worked-solution "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {8}^{x}+12x+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\cdot {8}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(12x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({8}^{x})+12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8){8}^{x})+12(1)+0 \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8){8}^{x}+12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186296661 :answer-field/correct "answer-f54d10f9-87ce-520f-be5c-16afa4e5c6a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f54d10f9-87ce-520f-be5c-16afa4e5c6a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f54d10f9-87ce-520f-be5c-16afa4e5c6a2" :answer/id #uuid "f54d10f9-87ce-520f-be5c-16afa4e5c6a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\cdot8^{x}\\ln(8)+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097815 :tutorial/content "To derive the identity\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(e^x) = e^x,\n$$\n\nwe begin with the definition of the derivative:\n\nwhere $f(x) = e^x$.\n\nSubstituting the function $f(x)$ into the definition of $f'(x),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x+h}-{e}^{x}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{h}-{e}^{x}}{h} \\\\  & ={lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot ({e}^{h}-1)}{h} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {lim}_{h\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{h}-1}{h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, it can be shown that\n\n$$\n\\lim_{h \\to 0} \\frac{e^h - 1}{h} = 1,\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\nf'(x) = e^x \\cdot 1 = e^x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}(e^x) = e^x.\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096892 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221456 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9b306e59-ac03-5a23-8563-3ae450882f03" "question-234b7e73-d01a-5fb8-b7f2-7b7733987672"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-9b306e59-ac03-5a23-8563-3ae450882f03" :question/id #uuid "9b306e59-ac03-5a23-8563-3ae450882f03" :question/math-academy-id "q-343882" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-5y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the cosine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})-5(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))=5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-5\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})=5+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and sine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=5 \\\\ {b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-5)=\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-1 \\\\ {b}_{n}=-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e37207bf-0563-5832-ad30-c6a23c3c930c" "answer-field-8f9455a9-07ca-5997-b4ca-16fa2b6ab07c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e37207bf-0563-5832-ad30-c6a23c3c930c" :answer-field/id #uuid "e37207bf-0563-5832-ad30-c6a23c3c930c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-35c42206-68dd-51fc-99b6-ae210d259dac" :answer-field/choices ["answer-35c42206-68dd-51fc-99b6-ae210d259dac" "answer-8c0a8364-45bf-574e-bb9d-0ac0a859448d" "answer-cf0bdb29-be00-5a7a-ae5b-f5917ddd3a3f" "answer-3b2f4c1a-00a1-55c0-9e44-6bcc54f3f7de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35c42206-68dd-51fc-99b6-ae210d259dac" :answer/id #uuid "35c42206-68dd-51fc-99b6-ae210d259dac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c0a8364-45bf-574e-bb9d-0ac0a859448d" :answer/id #uuid "8c0a8364-45bf-574e-bb9d-0ac0a859448d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf0bdb29-be00-5a7a-ae5b-f5917ddd3a3f" :answer/id #uuid "cf0bdb29-be00-5a7a-ae5b-f5917ddd3a3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b2f4c1a-00a1-55c0-9e44-6bcc54f3f7de" :answer/id #uuid "3b2f4c1a-00a1-55c0-9e44-6bcc54f3f7de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f9455a9-07ca-5997-b4ca-16fa2b6ab07c" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f9455a9-07ca-5997-b4ca-16fa2b6ab07c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4e4cc218-73fe-5998-8ccf-bc16f3b90e09" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e570c1cd-6353-5178-af72-bcd3aab8e4d9" "answer-b9355ba0-889c-5450-99e3-818ab0a4f2f1" "answer-4e4cc218-73fe-5998-8ccf-bc16f3b90e09" "answer-d0a1ae82-6bda-5f83-b1fc-96118fbd6f97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e570c1cd-6353-5178-af72-bcd3aab8e4d9" :answer/id #uuid "e570c1cd-6353-5178-af72-bcd3aab8e4d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9355ba0-889c-5450-99e3-818ab0a4f2f1" :answer/id #uuid "b9355ba0-889c-5450-99e3-818ab0a4f2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e4cc218-73fe-5998-8ccf-bc16f3b90e09" :answer/id #uuid "4e4cc218-73fe-5998-8ccf-bc16f3b90e09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d0a1ae82-6bda-5f83-b1fc-96118fbd6f97" :answer/id #uuid "d0a1ae82-6bda-5f83-b1fc-96118fbd6f97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+20)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-234b7e73-d01a-5fb8-b7f2-7b7733987672" :question/id #uuid "234b7e73-d01a-5fb8-b7f2-7b7733987672" :question/math-academy-id "q-343886" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-10y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼10+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the cosine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{{b}_{n}n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-\\frac{{b}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})-10(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}))=10+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-10\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-10)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})=10+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and sine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-10\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=10 \\\\ {b}_{n}(-\\frac{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-10)=\\frac{5(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}=-1 \\\\ {b}_{n}=\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-04a2bae6-aeac-5a01-8bbe-2da7affb6702" "answer-field-3b8556e9-1a54-5d0b-a5a5-5efa77eeb553"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-04a2bae6-aeac-5a01-8bbe-2da7affb6702" :answer-field/id #uuid "04a2bae6-aeac-5a01-8bbe-2da7affb6702" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-86854eda-5a8f-50ea-94b0-dd55b64266ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-86854eda-5a8f-50ea-94b0-dd55b64266ee" "answer-ed1a145b-0c0c-558c-963e-71228c0de2a2" "answer-344d0e42-cd70-5ad8-90fc-7db764816086" "answer-ce713a1f-b2ec-53d9-97c8-17515419704d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86854eda-5a8f-50ea-94b0-dd55b64266ee" :answer/id #uuid "86854eda-5a8f-50ea-94b0-dd55b64266ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed1a145b-0c0c-558c-963e-71228c0de2a2" :answer/id #uuid "ed1a145b-0c0c-558c-963e-71228c0de2a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-344d0e42-cd70-5ad8-90fc-7db764816086" :answer/id #uuid "344d0e42-cd70-5ad8-90fc-7db764816086" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce713a1f-b2ec-53d9-97c8-17515419704d" :answer/id #uuid "ce713a1f-b2ec-53d9-97c8-17515419704d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b8556e9-1a54-5d0b-a5a5-5efa77eeb553" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b8556e9-1a54-5d0b-a5a5-5efa77eeb553" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ae2ce446-0043-5cc6-9d9f-038477aa3b6a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-05e74e00-5bf0-5bcb-9c73-5ac12785eb89" "answer-20391762-3990-5977-9275-05105acc9764" "answer-ae2ce446-0043-5cc6-9d9f-038477aa3b6a" "answer-96006c5e-26f2-501a-82c3-1c733fab3f3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05e74e00-5bf0-5bcb-9c73-5ac12785eb89" :answer/id #uuid "05e74e00-5bf0-5bcb-9c73-5ac12785eb89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20391762-3990-5977-9275-05105acc9764" :answer/id #uuid "20391762-3990-5977-9275-05105acc9764" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae2ce446-0043-5cc6-9d9f-038477aa3b6a" :answer/id #uuid "ae2ce446-0043-5cc6-9d9f-038477aa3b6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96006c5e-26f2-501a-82c3-1c733fab3f3f" :answer/id #uuid "96006c5e-26f2-501a-82c3-1c733fab3f3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+40)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221457 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1741c2e1-8000-5ded-a8b9-94a357d2c64a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1741c2e1-8000-5ded-a8b9-94a357d2c64a" :question/id #uuid "1741c2e1-8000-5ded-a8b9-94a357d2c64a" :question/math-academy-id "q-343887" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=f(x),$ where the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $4$-periodic function $(L=2)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFor $n=3$, we have ${\\omega }_{3}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ Since ${\\omega }_{3}=\\omega ,$ the $n=3$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=3$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{3}(x)=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{3}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}))+x(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{3\\pi }{2}B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″} & =-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{3}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}):$\n\n$$\n[-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{3}}]+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})=\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3\\pi A=0 \\\\ 3\\pi B=\\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}A=0 \\\\ B=\\frac{1}{27\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-65f9587c-2102-51c3-9018-cf73e669ee77" "answer-field-b41532f6-c5f8-55db-9dde-0e3b62dd91b0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-65f9587c-2102-51c3-9018-cf73e669ee77" :answer-field/id #uuid "65f9587c-2102-51c3-9018-cf73e669ee77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-dbf1af4e-c02d-5acb-a898-ed1acac8e812" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a69c5953-f455-53cf-a745-4db7c010554c" "answer-11f6e6ae-3c6c-50c6-99cc-458271767c9c" "answer-dbf1af4e-c02d-5acb-a898-ed1acac8e812" "answer-075ff70c-8adb-53e9-8868-dac30ec95b33"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a69c5953-f455-53cf-a745-4db7c010554c" :answe