" :activity/id #uuid "faee6521-d29c-5e69-8077-dd4f40c45a4d" :activity/title "Calculating Global Extrema of Multivariable Functions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048450 :activity/course 17592186046644 :activity/steps ["step-edf9a3f1-f1e7-5cb6-855c-9ad5ddf8f9e0" "step-eab0fb9f-c4e9-5efc-b37f-9403a6a4f3b2" "step-35938dae-f811-5e2e-ad95-963a9aa094b9" "step-9f68dbce-6e45-599a-bfd1-c6b275925b2a" "step-fb52dde0-9ad8-55d6-b552-eb2fb08647fe"] :activity/first-step "step-edf9a3f1-f1e7-5cb6-855c-9ad5ddf8f9e0" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-edf9a3f1-f1e7-5cb6-855c-9ad5ddf8f9e0" :step/id #uuid "edf9a3f1-f1e7-5cb6-855c-9ad5ddf8f9e0" :step/content 17592186446484 :step/next "step-eab0fb9f-c4e9-5efc-b37f-9403a6a4f3b2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eab0fb9f-c4e9-5efc-b37f-9403a6a4f3b2" :step/id #uuid "eab0fb9f-c4e9-5efc-b37f-9403a6a4f3b2" :step/content 17592186446479 :step/next "step-35938dae-f811-5e2e-ad95-963a9aa094b9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-35938dae-f811-5e2e-ad95-963a9aa094b9" :step/id #uuid "35938dae-f811-5e2e-ad95-963a9aa094b9" :step/content 17592186446487 :step/next "step-9f68dbce-6e45-599a-bfd1-c6b275925b2a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-9f68dbce-6e45-599a-bfd1-c6b275925b2a" :step/id #uuid "9f68dbce-6e45-599a-bfd1-c6b275925b2a" :step/content 17592186446485 :step/next "step-fb52dde0-9ad8-55d6-b552-eb2fb08647fe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fb52dde0-9ad8-55d6-b552-eb2fb08647fe" :step/id #uuid "fb52dde0-9ad8-55d6-b552-eb2fb08647fe" :step/content 17592186401579 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156976] [:db/retract 17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156977] [:db/retract 17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156978] [:db/retract 17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156979] [:db/retract 17592186156975 :answer-field/choices 17592186156980] {:db/id 17592186157375 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-9d9e7f8d-7ad5-5408-a4ca-eaab80943f96" "question-e042f50a-1181-570f-8ece-0feac63fb8cc" "question-04a40517-0aa4-5398-b54b-804112b670f0" "question-e55c9ea3-689a-5b3d-8e62-79deec4589d4" "question-75c2a299-1223-5668-b631-6cae0200f484"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157195 :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the duration of the radio program. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U[27,34],$ and we wish to compute $P(X < 30).$\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/2a/2a615c021abbdd4009eb1debcda9b9c3076f6a9f087c6e1e6fd9454b9334eb17.svg)\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U[27,34],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/93/938214f94631d071b2bcd6b672e3b9b903918a88676da2cdc3b978cd94d891b2.svg)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<30) & ={\\int }_{27}^{30}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{27}^{30}\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{7}|}_{27}^{30} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{7}-\\frac{27}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157376 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a26697c2-b707-5c92-9d4e-fbd65d029113" "question-1aba9da0-33cd-5e33-a9f2-c4176a10b635" "question-1e4d63bb-964b-5518-80b3-c4adef9c4173" "question-dde847bc-5ddb-54de-88c5-81b18b2aa0d0" "question-34de765e-8b52-5fc4-a07d-973bddb6d3ad"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157196 :question/problem "A video game randomly generates an obstacle the player has to avoid. The obstacle's $x$-coordinate is uniformly distributed along a segment whose endpoints have $x$-coordinates of $-6$ and $12.$ What is the mean $x$-coordinate of the obstacle?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the $x$-coordinate of a randomly generated obstacle. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U[-6,12],$ and we wish to compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U[-6,12],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{-6+12}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean $x$-coordinate is $3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157377 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ad59302d-b27c-5dd6-8065-5abc6de41bf0" "question-881664f0-8e9c-5727-bbea-b101cf17a4b3" "question-b676f753-31e2-5fb5-a7e2-ab7b8253e6c3" "question-fefe1132-ca93-5e93-921e-5c1fd45e5581"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157197 :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the visiting time of a randomly chosen visitor. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U[1.5,4.5],$ and we wish to compute $\\textrm{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(b-a)^2}{12}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U[1.5,4.5],$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{(4.5-1.5)^2}{12} = \\dfrac{9}{12} = \\dfrac{3}{4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is $\\dfrac{3}{4}\\,\\textrm{hr}^2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-9d9e7f8d-7ad5-5408-a4ca-eaab80943f96" :question/id #uuid "9d9e7f8d-7ad5-5408-a4ca-eaab80943f96" :question/math-academy-id "q-96870" :question/problem "The minimum time it takes an electrician to fix a power outage is $20$ minutes, and the maximum time is $160$ minutes. Assuming that the time it takes to fix the power outage is uniformly distributed, what is the probability that a random power outage fix takes more than $30$ minutes but less than $60$ minutes?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the time it takes to fix a random power outage. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[20,160],$ and we wish to compute $P(30<X<60).$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a}, & a\\le x\\le b \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[20,160],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{140}, & 20\\le x\\le 160 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(30<X<60) & ={\\int }_{30}^{60}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{30}^{60}\\frac{1}{140}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{140}|}_{30}^{60} \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{140}-\\frac{30}{140} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-91eb2137-924b-5cda-97be-891267d62252"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-91eb2137-924b-5cda-97be-891267d62252" :answer-field/id #uuid "91eb2137-924b-5cda-97be-891267d62252" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d6c5dd60-da56-5120-ac2a-e485b14f6897" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7442854e-4eef-58d2-937e-b8a32847ad0a" "answer-51db8527-e691-524a-8d64-0cecd1ce2030" "answer-891c8039-b5b1-5884-8dca-6e836ef55867" "answer-d6c5dd60-da56-5120-ac2a-e485b14f6897" "answer-7664a506-7a27-5659-88f7-2a7981b1344c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7442854e-4eef-58d2-937e-b8a32847ad0a" :answer/id #uuid "7442854e-4eef-58d2-937e-b8a32847ad0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51db8527-e691-524a-8d64-0cecd1ce2030" :answer/id #uuid "51db8527-e691-524a-8d64-0cecd1ce2030" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-891c8039-b5b1-5884-8dca-6e836ef55867" :answer/id #uuid "891c8039-b5b1-5884-8dca-6e836ef55867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{140}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6c5dd60-da56-5120-ac2a-e485b14f6897" :answer/id #uuid "d6c5dd60-da56-5120-ac2a-e485b14f6897" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7664a506-7a27-5659-88f7-2a7981b1344c" :answer/id #uuid "7664a506-7a27-5659-88f7-2a7981b1344c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e042f50a-1181-570f-8ece-0feac63fb8cc" :question/id #uuid "e042f50a-1181-570f-8ece-0feac63fb8cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-96859" :question/problem "A computer program is designed so that it can randomly generate a real number between $0$ and $10,$ inclusive. What is the probability that the number generated is between $3$ and $7?$" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number generated by the program. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[0,10],$ and we wish to compute $P(3<X<7).$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a}, & a\\le x\\le b \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[0,10],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10}, & 0\\le x\\le 10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3<X<7) & ={\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{7}\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{10}|}_{3}^{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}-\\frac{3}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e761c330-86b4-51d2-b2a4-8c7d84a3cd9a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e761c330-86b4-51d2-b2a4-8c7d84a3cd9a" :answer-field/id #uuid "e761c330-86b4-51d2-b2a4-8c7d84a3cd9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d80e92db-3cf5-5e65-b11c-1182c3250e87" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f6767626-734c-5b0e-a601-dd3d629fe5ed" "answer-d80e92db-3cf5-5e65-b11c-1182c3250e87" "answer-552517bf-8975-5614-bc42-fbfb2782e608" "answer-be80291f-0de3-5c39-a291-04b336487ab4" "answer-00062ecf-0f51-5e19-9310-d192161a5246"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6767626-734c-5b0e-a601-dd3d629fe5ed" :answer/id #uuid "f6767626-734c-5b0e-a601-dd3d629fe5ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d80e92db-3cf5-5e65-b11c-1182c3250e87" :answer/id #uuid "d80e92db-3cf5-5e65-b11c-1182c3250e87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-552517bf-8975-5614-bc42-fbfb2782e608" :answer/id #uuid "552517bf-8975-5614-bc42-fbfb2782e608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be80291f-0de3-5c39-a291-04b336487ab4" :answer/id #uuid "be80291f-0de3-5c39-a291-04b336487ab4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-00062ecf-0f51-5e19-9310-d192161a5246" :answer/id #uuid "00062ecf-0f51-5e19-9310-d192161a5246" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-04a40517-0aa4-5398-b54b-804112b670f0" :question/id #uuid "04a40517-0aa4-5398-b54b-804112b670f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96739" :question/problem "The distance covered per game by a particular soccer player is uniformly distributed between $10\\,\\text{km}$\n and $13\\,\\text{km}$ inclusive. What is the probability that this player runs $12\\,\\text{km}$ or more in a randomly selected game?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the distance covered by the player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[10,13],$ and we wish to compute $P(X\\ge 12).$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a}, & a\\le x\\le b \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[10,13],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & 10\\le x\\le 13 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 12) & ={\\int }_{12}^{13}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{12}^{13}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{3}|}_{12}^{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{3}-\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-56c85a06-4467-5818-826d-ae5c1ae05ad9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-56c85a06-4467-5818-826d-ae5c1ae05ad9" :answer-field/id #uuid "56c85a06-4467-5818-826d-ae5c1ae05ad9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-53da8f36-10c8-5cc6-86e4-472caa08a221" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dfba38fe-2d5e-512c-9841-9b766813abf6" "answer-9816d79b-cb35-5e33-8ecc-f8d36301c91e" "answer-2bda0597-d4eb-501c-8f78-9cc0d69850ff" "answer-53da8f36-10c8-5cc6-86e4-472caa08a221" "answer-5609f0e7-a55f-54bb-b60f-a7f0957c755b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfba38fe-2d5e-512c-9841-9b766813abf6" :answer/id #uuid "dfba38fe-2d5e-512c-9841-9b766813abf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9816d79b-cb35-5e33-8ecc-f8d36301c91e" :answer/id #uuid "9816d79b-cb35-5e33-8ecc-f8d36301c91e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bda0597-d4eb-501c-8f78-9cc0d69850ff" :answer/id #uuid "2bda0597-d4eb-501c-8f78-9cc0d69850ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53da8f36-10c8-5cc6-86e4-472caa08a221" :answer/id #uuid "53da8f36-10c8-5cc6-86e4-472caa08a221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5609f0e7-a55f-54bb-b60f-a7f0957c755b" :answer/id #uuid "5609f0e7-a55f-54bb-b60f-a7f0957c755b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e55c9ea3-689a-5b3d-8e62-79deec4589d4" :question/id #uuid "e55c9ea3-689a-5b3d-8e62-79deec4589d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-96738" :question/problem "The duration of a tv program is uniformly distributed between $52$ and $66$ minutes, inclusive. What is the probability that a randomly chosen program lasts $60$ minutes or less?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the duration of the tv program. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[52,66],$ and we wish to compute $P(X\\le 60).$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a}, & a\\le x\\le b \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[52,66],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{14}, & 52\\le x\\le 66 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 60) & ={\\int }_{52}^{60}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{52}^{60}\\frac{1}{14}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{14}|}_{52}^{60} \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{14}-\\frac{52}{14} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cca69172-8d2b-50ee-94f0-4248d1848b28"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cca69172-8d2b-50ee-94f0-4248d1848b28" :answer-field/id #uuid "cca69172-8d2b-50ee-94f0-4248d1848b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1250b344-6a3f-5e22-8259-6b6f4e1fd664" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1883d56-92de-539c-8f2f-861ea03c9e84" "answer-b0fdf54d-8e0d-564f-bace-2883c73dc5d0" "answer-3b42918c-1af0-5846-b7eb-f58a3c71f7d7" "answer-1250b344-6a3f-5e22-8259-6b6f4e1fd664" "answer-f040bfd2-f972-53d7-af55-e0a4c410abc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1883d56-92de-539c-8f2f-861ea03c9e84" :answer/id #uuid "d1883d56-92de-539c-8f2f-861ea03c9e84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0fdf54d-8e0d-564f-bace-2883c73dc5d0" :answer/id #uuid "b0fdf54d-8e0d-564f-bace-2883c73dc5d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b42918c-1af0-5846-b7eb-f58a3c71f7d7" :answer/id #uuid "3b42918c-1af0-5846-b7eb-f58a3c71f7d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1250b344-6a3f-5e22-8259-6b6f4e1fd664" :answer/id #uuid "1250b344-6a3f-5e22-8259-6b6f4e1fd664" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f040bfd2-f972-53d7-af55-e0a4c410abc4" :answer/id #uuid "f040bfd2-f972-53d7-af55-e0a4c410abc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-75c2a299-1223-5668-b631-6cae0200f484" :question/id #uuid "75c2a299-1223-5668-b631-6cae0200f484" :question/math-academy-id "q-170687" :question/problem "In an online poker tournament, the maximum loss is $10$ dollars, and the maximum win is $8$ dollars. Assuming that a player's earnings are uniformly distributed between $-10$ and $8,$ what is the probability that a randomly chosen player loses between $2$ and $8$ dollars?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the earnings of a randomly chosen player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[-10,8],$ and we wish to compute $P(-8\\le X\\le -2).$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a}, & a\\le x\\le b \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[-10,8],$ we have the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}, & -10\\le x\\le 8 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-8\\le X\\le -2) & ={\\int }_{-8}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-8}^{-2}\\frac{1}{18}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{x}{18}|}_{-8}^{-2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{18}-(-\\frac{8}{18}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-11562c89-3fe2-5b73-bf46-55642d35bb9e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-11562c89-3fe2-5b73-bf46-55642d35bb9e" :answer-field/id #uuid "11562c89-3fe2-5b73-bf46-55642d35bb9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ba99982b-5521-5081-812d-09016da48ec3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ba99982b-5521-5081-812d-09016da48ec3" "answer-694234a6-597f-5e61-b5bf-84fc5b6aa6e5" "answer-0f89f754-b00e-5b7c-b63f-401fe4f471d6" "answer-6c3f9669-23d7-5243-84e9-d09de434a07d" "answer-a7c0d009-d03a-5fb2-a0bd-6539af2c96d7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba99982b-5521-5081-812d-09016da48ec3" :answer/id #uuid "ba99982b-5521-5081-812d-09016da48ec3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-694234a6-597f-5e61-b5bf-84fc5b6aa6e5" :answer/id #uuid "694234a6-597f-5e61-b5bf-84fc5b6aa6e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f89f754-b00e-5b7c-b63f-401fe4f471d6" :answer/id #uuid "0f89f754-b00e-5b7c-b63f-401fe4f471d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c3f9669-23d7-5243-84e9-d09de434a07d" :answer/id #uuid "6c3f9669-23d7-5243-84e9-d09de434a07d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7c0d009-d03a-5fb2-a0bd-6539af2c96d7" :answer/id #uuid "a7c0d009-d03a-5fb2-a0bd-6539af2c96d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{18}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a26697c2-b707-5c92-9d4e-fbd65d029113" :question/id #uuid "a26697c2-b707-5c92-9d4e-fbd65d029113" :question/math-academy-id "q-170689" :question/problem "The return on a risky investment can be negative (meaning that the investor loses money) or positive. Assuming that the return on a particular investment is uniformly distributed between $-7.5%$ and $12.5%$, what is the mean return of this investment?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the return on the investment. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[-7.5,12.5],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[-7.5,12.5],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{-7.5+12.5}{2}=2.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean return on the investment is $2.5%.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7f1ec29c-42d2-57fd-ab8f-09eebbc31a36"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7f1ec29c-42d2-57fd-ab8f-09eebbc31a36" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1ec29c-42d2-57fd-ab8f-09eebbc31a36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a98338f2-91a3-5fd0-b05b-41b44d5b2088" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3be5c8b5-28f2-5645-b875-656ae6aa32d1" "answer-f6815909-1c16-57b5-8a29-b68e399a5fc1" "answer-a98338f2-91a3-5fd0-b05b-41b44d5b2088" "answer-82c1f078-7b17-5093-a2b1-e9a218c6e391" "answer-bafe428e-9edd-5e95-bef2-1daa264b46f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3be5c8b5-28f2-5645-b875-656ae6aa32d1" :answer/id #uuid "3be5c8b5-28f2-5645-b875-656ae6aa32d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2.5%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6815909-1c16-57b5-8a29-b68e399a5fc1" :answer/id #uuid "f6815909-1c16-57b5-8a29-b68e399a5fc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a98338f2-91a3-5fd0-b05b-41b44d5b2088" :answer/id #uuid "a98338f2-91a3-5fd0-b05b-41b44d5b2088" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82c1f078-7b17-5093-a2b1-e9a218c6e391" :answer/id #uuid "82c1f078-7b17-5093-a2b1-e9a218c6e391" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bafe428e-9edd-5e95-bef2-1daa264b46f4" :answer/id #uuid "bafe428e-9edd-5e95-bef2-1daa264b46f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.25%" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1aba9da0-33cd-5e33-a9f2-c4176a10b635" :question/id #uuid "1aba9da0-33cd-5e33-a9f2-c4176a10b635" :question/math-academy-id "q-96912" :question/problem "The distance covered by a basketball player in an official match is uniformly distributed between $3$ and $4$ km, inclusive. What is the mean distance covered per match?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the distance covered by a randomly chosen basketball player. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[3,4],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[3,4],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3+4}{2}=3.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean distance covered is $3.5\\,\\text{km}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c93f235b-793b-55f7-ab41-4624f17dc702"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c93f235b-793b-55f7-ab41-4624f17dc702" :answer-field/id #uuid "c93f235b-793b-55f7-ab41-4624f17dc702" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c09a2f15-28c9-5ffe-af6b-aec2c59a2452" :answer-field/choices ["answer-370a6f48-1321-598d-961d-21215c99efae" "answer-ed0fd3e2-7218-5a55-b3ea-6212dfbbcea4" "answer-c09a2f15