an battery duration is $25\\,\\text{hrs}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0bdc12ec-cffe-5433-a8cf-eda9a9bc5849"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0bdc12ec-cffe-5433-a8cf-eda9a9bc5849" :answer-field/id #uuid "0bdc12ec-cffe-5433-a8cf-eda9a9bc5849" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-db3e02b0-3400-5f28-9333-791ec7386ccd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdcf88ff-a820-57d4-93f4-c6c1bb73cdc7" "answer-db3e02b0-3400-5f28-9333-791ec7386ccd" "answer-6eb9fe59-d227-5978-bc0e-8c3248818cd3" "answer-6fc67d2e-104d-517e-b7ad-3963058d50e7" "answer-da20904d-6f33-5883-b6a2-506ba44d56ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdcf88ff-a820-57d4-93f4-c6c1bb73cdc7" :answer/id #uuid "fdcf88ff-a820-57d4-93f4-c6c1bb73cdc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\,\\text{hrs}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db3e02b0-3400-5f28-9333-791ec7386ccd" :answer/id #uuid "db3e02b0-3400-5f28-9333-791ec7386ccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\,\\text{hrs}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6eb9fe59-d227-5978-bc0e-8c3248818cd3" :answer/id #uuid "6eb9fe59-d227-5978-bc0e-8c3248818cd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\,\\text{hrs}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fc67d2e-104d-517e-b7ad-3963058d50e7" :answer/id #uuid "6fc67d2e-104d-517e-b7ad-3963058d50e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35\\,\\text{hrs}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da20904d-6f33-5883-b6a2-506ba44d56ea" :answer/id #uuid "da20904d-6f33-5883-b6a2-506ba44d56ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50\\,\\text{hrs}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-dde847bc-5ddb-54de-88c5-81b18b2aa0d0" :question/id #uuid "dde847bc-5ddb-54de-88c5-81b18b2aa0d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96915" :question/problem "The height of water in a dam is uniformly distributed between $120$ and $195$ meters, inclusive. What is the mean height of the water?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the height of water in a random inspection of the dam. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[120,195],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[120,195],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{120+195}{2}=157.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean height of water in the dam is $157.5\\,\\text{m}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b332393b-467d-57f6-86e8-201567c24b59"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b332393b-467d-57f6-86e8-201567c24b59" :answer-field/id #uuid "b332393b-467d-57f6-86e8-201567c24b59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ff61f4a5-fdc7-50ac-8e2e-f37f8b83242a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5881b8aa-fa36-5d7c-81f9-47ae6f95c700" "answer-2e690e66-2b08-578a-8669-8a4559b8135b" "answer-ff61f4a5-fdc7-50ac-8e2e-f37f8b83242a" "answer-540a4c2f-1c8b-54a6-871e-f1146cfd3188" "answer-654974a1-1f54-5eaa-88ed-8f82bc70ce92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5881b8aa-fa36-5d7c-81f9-47ae6f95c700" :answer/id #uuid "5881b8aa-fa36-5d7c-81f9-47ae6f95c700" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e690e66-2b08-578a-8669-8a4559b8135b" :answer/id #uuid "2e690e66-2b08-578a-8669-8a4559b8135b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "155.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ff61f4a5-fdc7-50ac-8e2e-f37f8b83242a" :answer/id #uuid "ff61f4a5-fdc7-50ac-8e2e-f37f8b83242a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "157.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-540a4c2f-1c8b-54a6-871e-f1146cfd3188" :answer/id #uuid "540a4c2f-1c8b-54a6-871e-f1146cfd3188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "195\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-654974a1-1f54-5eaa-88ed-8f82bc70ce92" :answer/id #uuid "654974a1-1f54-5eaa-88ed-8f82bc70ce92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "315\\,\\text{m}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-34de765e-8b52-5fc4-a07d-973bddb6d3ad" :question/id #uuid "34de765e-8b52-5fc4-a07d-973bddb6d3ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-96922" :question/problem "The minimum time it takes a plumber to fix a leaky pipe is $30$ minutes, and the maximum time is $110$ minutes.  Assuming that the plumber's time to fix a leaky pipe is uniformly distributed, what is the expected time to fix a pipe?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the time to fix a randomly chosen leaky pipe. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U[30,110],$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U[a,b],$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U[30,110],$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{30+110}{2}=70\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean time to fix the leaky pipe is $70\\,\\text{min}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/id #uuid "f297313b-3683-5d45-a02e-e17a9c10bf9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04369663-ee6d-5779-b279-d5950bae1b5d" "answer-8d155fe7-b1b6-53a9-84dc-0848f037b735" "answer-91b4c9f3-7029-518f-ba7e-e5cb07c0455c" "answer-df6a5038-8e94-596d-8743-3127d9d275c4" "answer-c007a719-a2a8-5a6d-a919-b4ccf57175e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04369663-ee6d-5779-b279-